is  half-brother lortz's real father yeah it  starts to get a bit complicated this  causes a rift between the two to the  point  magna denounces his chosen one status  and losing his powers couldn't come at a  worse time in old norse tradition it is  up to the sun to avenge the father  so fiore having the power of the giants  sets his eyes on killing magna fiore  also ends up taking over util industries  something his sister  saxa resents since she wanted that  position but we'll get more into that  later but even without his powers magna  decides to join the team into breaking  into util industries in search of the  eternal fire  the only flame that can forge mjolnir  the weapon which will defeat the giants  in the battle of ragnarok in order to  craft mjolnir they'll need a few things  a feather head and spear tip from the  old world and a dwarf to forge it  the feather is what gives the hammer its  ability to fly and return  back to thor harry who is really the  embodiment of the war god tear is the  muscle fighting off fjord and getting  his hand chopped off in the process  in norse mythology tyr only has one hand  the other having been ripped off by the  wolf fenrir magda's ability to gain  access to the flame wouldn't have been  possible if it weren't for his brother  lords  lords was given the key to the warehouse  by saxa who at this point in the story  really hates her family for ousting her  as president of util industries  saxon never knew that lords would end up  giving the key to magna and magna even  lied to lawrence about what he was going  to do with it  you can see it gets a little bit  complicated magda lies to lorite saying  he needs the key to impress a girl  sidney telling him that he plans to hang  a big fu to util industry sign he knows  he can't tell his brother the truth that  he's about to forge a weapon that will  kill his biological family and could  potentially kill loritz himself  lawrence arguably has one of the biggest  emotional arcs this season an arc which  sets him up as the trickster god loki  at the beginning of the season lorettz  learns that his mother had an affair  with vedar making him the son of a giant  and half brother to magna this puts him  in a difficult position because his  biological dad is a giant and is half  brother  a god who does he side with and things  get more complicated when it seems  everyone around him betrays him  including bran who tries to kill him  this sets him up perfectly as loki as  you're never really sure what side he's  on or what trick he has up his sleeve  and if things weren't crazy enough lortz  injects himself with odin's blood in  norse mythology odin and loki were blood  brothers who swore a blood oath making  loki truly unique in this way loki  really becomes  half god half giant the implications of  this haven't been fully realized in the  show just yet  lord's journey this season also sees him  give birth to jormungandr  or the midgard serpent in norse  mythology it is said this serpent grew  so large it was able to surround the  earth and grasp its own tail  at which time ragnarok would begin the  serpent's arch enemy  is thor thor ultimately killing it these  clues help us see where these storylines  could take us in future seasons in  mythology it's never really explained  how loki gave birth to the snake  but in the show the snake is surgically  removed after being diagnosed as a  tapeworm in lawrence just how loritz  came to acquire this tapeworm is also  not known however we do know it started  to grow  shortly after he had his outing with  vidar in which he ate a raw reindeer  heart and was shown his healing powers  the final episode is titled all you need  is love the line lord says to magna  after being convinced magnus using the  key for love  the irony here is that it's magna's love  for his brother not  cygni that is making him forge the  hammer magda is able to successfully  forge it and escape  running home just in time for his 18th  birthday  he tries throwing it just like he did in  season one but his powers have not  returned  meanwhile iman and halva are fired from  their jobs at the troll garden nursing  home where voton is a patient he and the  other patients give them a rousing  send-off of yes we love this country  which is the norwegian national anthem  and same song that played in the last  episode of season 1.  tour does magna to gather lords's  laundry where he discovers lords has  been keeping this snake  it's kind of interesting since if the  show follows the mythology it will be  him who eventually kills it lawrence  picks up burgers for magna's birthday  where he finds out his love interest who  works at the diner is making  out with the epa officer it's just  another instance that showcases how  loritz is so  alone by the end of the season he'll  have been betrayed by his brother  ostracized by the giants and heartbroken  by his crush this sets up his character  to be one who only cares about himself  over the past few episodes magna has  been struggling with a paper on norse  mythology and eventually asked the  question  tusha  a classic what came first the chicken or  the egg when it starts to thunder  magnus hammer begins to rumble  which is coincidentally the same line i  say to my romantic partners  unlike a few episodes ago magna has  embraced who he is the chosen one and  only when he realizes this do his powers  come back to him  lawrence does not approve believing that  magna's betrayal and forging of the  hammer brings him  one step closer to killing him  ron and fiore punished saxa after all it  could only have been her key that opened  the warehouse  this beating along with her ousting as  president of util will see her  allegiance  shift with his powers back magna heads  to the utils where he'll find  saxa beaten up and in one of the  strangest turns of the season  saxa offers an alliance of sorts saying  that the two of them together could rule  everything she'd be able to take over  yutal and he'd be able to kill ran and  fiore she then attempts to grab magnus  hammer before  grabbing his other hammer yes saxa and  magna make love i personally felt this  turn  wasn't quite earned in the show but i  can see what the writers were trying to  do here because  in norse mythology saxa is a lover of  thor  and ends up birthing two of his sons  modi and magni  she never becomes thor's monogamous  lover so expect a lot of drama to come  out of this relationship in season 3.  after they do have sex magna remarks how  it doesn't feel right and that's  probably because gods and giants are  arch enemies  and this isn't supposed to happen  meanwhile ran and fiore try to kill  loritz they believe he gave the key to  magna to forge the weapon that could  kill them  however they don't know that loritz was  tricked into this and just when it looks  like  lords will be a goner lord says he has  the one thing that can destroy magna for  good he's of course referring to the  world serpent they watch him release at  the end of the episode  magna arrives and uses his sick hammer  to chase off ren and fjor  he asks for lords's forgiveness which we  never get an  answer and in the final scene of the  season lords unleashes the rapidly  growing snake into the fjord as ran and  fiore watch on  the final shot being of lortz's amber  and blue eyes  signifying his half god half giant blood  now there's currently no word if  ragnarok has been greenlit for season 3  but it's clear season 2 has set up a ton  of potential storylines will gree come  back from the city will there be a time  jump how will the utils gain the upper  hand  and whose side will loki eventually  gravitate towards  i want to hear all your thoughts and  theories in the comments below thanks  for watching everyone please make sure  to like and subscribe it really means a  lot for me in the channel and for more  bad takes you can follow me on twitter  and instagram at thingstoryt  until next time remember daddy loves you  very much

